  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The new Live Now page has buttons to instantly join the instance that only appear when you hover. Its natural for people to want to click the thumbnail to expand the details, but then suddenly buttons right under your cursor, oops you're joining now, good luck! Hope you're on desktop and can Alt+F4!\n\nDon't you have analytics from the the Variety Box page that show that no human has ever intentionally clicked one of those join buttons? The Live Now page is slightly better because at least its not literally a random instance, but I can't believe you did it again. Haven't you people learned your lesson? Not even an \"Are you sure\" popup? Crimes against UX. Despicable.",
